Here you'll find the catalogue of available commands, grouped by category (utility, partnership, music, moderation and so on).

For each command you can typically:

• turn it on or off on the server;
• limit it to allowed channels or exclude channels;
• limit it to allowed roles or exclude roles;
• open the command help to understand what it does.

Rule of thumb: if you set «allowed» lists, the «ignored» lists of the same type should be considered as an alternative — don't mix opposite logics without a clear reason. The dashboard guides you on this.

Open Partnership on the server and follow the guided startup (if the server isn't ready yet).

In short you'll be asked to set:

• the partnership channel where published messages go;
• (optional) a log/activity channel;
• the role of the team that manages partnerships;
• any automatic notices with thresholds (mass pings or to a role), plus an optional delay between one “real” notice and the next.

Once done, later changes are made from the Partnership subsections (General, Filters, Embed, etc.), always from the dashboard.
